  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 5th March 2008, the continued use of 245 Vicarage Farm Road as three self-contained flats was not lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe evidence submitted does not establish that, on the balance of probabilities, the property has been continuously used as three flats for at least four years from the date of the current application for a Certificate of Lawfulness, being 24 July 2008, and the evidence supplied does not precisely and unambiguously establish that, on the balance of probabilities, the property was converted into three flats on or before 24 July 2004.\r\n"
